  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a given array AAA of length NNN, and a parameter KKK, we define f(A,K)f(A, K)f(A,K) in the following way:\n\n\n\nConsider a random experiment of the following type:\n\n\n\nRepeat the following action KKK times: choose an integer index iii uniformly at random from [1,N][1, N][1,N], and update Ai←Ai+1A_i \\leftarrow A_i + 1Ai​←Ai​+1.\nAfter all KKK updates, define P=A1×A2×…×ANP = A_1 \\times A_2 \\times \\ldots \\times A_NP=A1​×A2​×…×AN​.\n\n\n\nf(A,K)f(A, K)f(A,K) is defined as the expected value of PPP modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7 in above random experiment.\n\n\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN, and you have to answer QQQ queries of the following type:\n\n\nGiven LLL, RRR and KKK, find f(A[L,R],K)f(A[L, R], K)f(A[L,R],K) where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] denotes the subarray [AL,AL+1,AL+2,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, A_{L + 2}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,AL+2​,…,AR​].\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 integers - NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe iii-th of the next QQQ lines contains 333 integers - L,RL, RL,R and KKK, the parameters for the iii-th query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, for each query, print f(A[L,R],K)f(A[L, R], K)f(A[L,R],K). As a reminder the expected values are to be printed modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,Q≤20001 \\le N, Q \\le 20001≤N,Q≤2000",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\le K \\le 10^91≤K≤109",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ both do not exceed 200020002000 over all test cases."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
